{
  "id": "punto_guajiro_cubano",
  "name": "Punto guajiro (Cuban improvised décima song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Sung poetry of the Cuban countryside, in which singers, often improvising, set ten-line décimas to traditional melodies (tonadas) accompanied by laúd, tres, guitar and light percussion such as güiro and claves; UNESCO inscribed Punto on its Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity. Punto libre, where the accompaniment drops out under the free-rhythm vocal line, is tied to the west of the island and punto fijo, in strict time, to the centre; the controversia is a sung duel of improvised décimas between two poets.",
  "recipe": "classic modern punto guajiro, ballad Poetry, Latin am troubadour branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment. laud cedar canonical Cuban octave doubled bronze steel rural traditional tres cubano, classical nylon-string guitar, claves, gourd wood guiro. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
